WEBVTT

00:37.537 --> 00:42.042
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE

01:48.399 --> 01:49.651
Would you like to order?

01:49.734 --> 01:51.736
Well,

01:53.196 --> 01:57.117
I'm here to see someone called Silverbill.

02:22.851 --> 02:28.022
It's been over ten days
since I lost contact with my son.

02:28.106 --> 02:30.608
You should talk to the police
about a runaway kid.

02:30.692 --> 02:32.068
He didn't run away.

02:33.778 --> 02:34.946
He's gone missing.

02:36.489 --> 02:38.700
MADAM NA

02:39.993 --> 02:40.994
Job request.

02:41.077 --> 02:44.497
Missing person's name, Oh Ki-hoon.
Age 29.

02:44.998 --> 02:46.958
He went missing about ten days ago.

02:49.836 --> 02:50.753
Do you accept?

03:35.673 --> 03:38.384
ACCEPTED

04:28.142 --> 04:30.728
How long are you going to keep this up?

04:34.899 --> 04:38.111
It's about time you moved on.

04:58.464 --> 05:02.385
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE
BETWEEN AWARENESS AND BLINDNESS

05:29.620 --> 05:31.748
Hi, Bugang Company's Jang Ho-jae speaking.

05:32.874 --> 05:36.794
EPISODE 1
HO-JAE

05:36.878 --> 05:40.131
BUGANG COMPANY
PIONEER OF GLOBAL COMMERCE

05:40.214 --> 05:42.800
BUGANG COMPANY
THE CENTER OF TRADE IN ASIA

05:42.884 --> 05:45.762
THE PRIDE OF JONGNO RETURNS ANEW

05:45.845 --> 05:49.891
CALL FOR ANY AND ALL REQUESTS
ON-CALL 24/7

06:00.860 --> 06:01.694
Going somewhere?

06:01.778 --> 06:04.197
I think we can obtain the evidence
Mr. Yang requested.

06:04.280 --> 06:05.365
Wait up.

06:05.948 --> 06:09.452
You should've told me that sooner, man.
We need to go together for that.

06:09.952 --> 06:11.037
I have to be there.

06:11.120 --> 06:13.831
Hey. You're the one going in today.

06:14.332 --> 06:16.542
What kind of nonsense is that?

06:16.626 --> 06:18.961
Let's stick to our traditions and rules.

06:19.045 --> 06:20.546
Settle it like we used to.

06:20.630 --> 06:21.547
Okay.

06:23.299 --> 06:24.217
Bring it on.

06:25.426 --> 06:28.137
- Cham cham cham!
- Cham cham cham!

06:29.972 --> 06:30.807
Settled.

06:31.307 --> 06:32.975
- Happy?
- Yeah.

06:33.476 --> 06:35.395
But you know what? I'll drive.

06:35.478 --> 06:36.396
Let's go.

06:37.230 --> 06:39.148
Cham cham cham.

06:39.232 --> 06:40.483
Why can't I win?

06:47.407 --> 06:48.825
That will be 6,800 won.

07:13.266 --> 07:17.562
Ho-jae, you know we have to pay off
the loan interest by this week, right?

07:17.645 --> 07:19.939
If you can't get a clear photo today,

07:20.606 --> 07:23.276
we won't get paid,
and the creditors will be onto us,

07:23.860 --> 07:27.488
which means the office will be seized
and we'll be out on the streets very soon.

07:27.572 --> 07:28.448
Hey,

07:29.240 --> 07:30.575
I always wondered…

07:30.658 --> 07:31.492
Yeah?

07:31.993 --> 07:35.663
Why do I have to pay the debt with you?
It has nothing to do with me.

07:35.746 --> 07:38.332
That's a good question.
How shall I put this?

07:38.416 --> 07:41.294
Because I'm the president of Bugang,
and you're the VP.

07:42.420 --> 07:43.504
Since when?

07:43.588 --> 07:45.590
Just put these on. Here.

07:47.884 --> 07:51.637
Hey, Bugang is the last business
that Grandpa left us.

07:51.721 --> 07:52.930
Who else would protect it?

07:53.014 --> 07:56.392
You, me, us!
We have to protect it together.

07:58.269 --> 08:01.397
Strictly speaking, he's your grandpa.
It's got nothing to do with me.

08:02.064 --> 08:04.442
You know how much Grandpa loved you.

08:04.525 --> 08:06.569
Well, I don't remember much about that.

08:06.652 --> 08:10.531
Besides, you and I don't have
anywhere else to be but Bugang.

08:10.615 --> 08:11.657
Speak for yourself.

08:12.158 --> 08:13.743
I'm in high demand.

08:14.994 --> 08:16.579
Cham cham… cham.

08:17.330 --> 08:18.164
See?

08:19.957 --> 08:22.585
Take this and go already.
And don't get caught.

08:22.668 --> 08:24.921
Go on. Hurry. Get to it.

08:25.880 --> 08:27.089
Come on!

08:27.173 --> 08:29.383
Hey, don't miss the face like last time.

08:30.593 --> 08:32.929
If the angle sucks,
we barely get half the pay!

08:33.429 --> 08:34.722
Love you, VP!

08:35.348 --> 08:37.558
Don't just capture the body. Get the face!

10:20.119 --> 10:21.287
Who's there?

11:36.862 --> 11:38.447
You're getting the feed, right?

11:39.615 --> 11:42.076
Of course I am. I made that thing.

12:13.149 --> 12:14.817
Why isn't anyone answering?

12:15.609 --> 12:16.777
Are they busy exercising?

12:16.861 --> 12:18.654
Don't be ridiculous.

12:18.738 --> 12:20.781
Are you sure it's room 608?

12:22.450 --> 12:23.868
Yeah, room 608.

12:24.744 --> 12:25.911
This is the room.

12:49.351 --> 12:51.604
I have a bad feeling about this.

12:51.687 --> 12:53.063
Should I abort for now?

12:53.147 --> 12:55.191
You can't do that, Ho-jae.

12:55.274 --> 12:57.777
You know we have
to pay the interest by this week.

12:57.860 --> 12:59.570
This is our only chance.

13:00.404 --> 13:02.740
We have to get the evidence today,
no matter what.

13:22.760 --> 13:24.887
Just barge in there, okay?

13:24.970 --> 13:27.598
Open the door
with the master key card I gave you,

13:27.681 --> 13:30.559
and just take one picture.
Then you're done, okay?

13:32.561 --> 13:34.730
Ho-jae, just do it. Please?

14:08.597 --> 14:09.849
There's no one here.

14:09.932 --> 14:12.852
Check the bathroom.
They might be taking a shower together.

14:28.117 --> 14:28.951
Shit!

14:33.956 --> 14:35.875
What the… Ho-jae?

14:51.891 --> 14:53.934
Is that… a woman?

15:16.832 --> 15:19.418
Sir! Room 608! There's an accident!

15:19.501 --> 15:21.170
- What?
- Hurry up! Come on!

16:02.544 --> 16:04.546
Hey, Ho-jae!

16:08.008 --> 16:10.719
Damn it!

16:11.428 --> 16:12.471
What in the…

16:15.599 --> 16:16.433
Why are you here?

16:17.893 --> 16:18.894
What are you doing?

16:19.478 --> 16:20.646
You said it was room 608.

16:20.729 --> 16:23.482
When did I say that? It was room 809!

16:31.907 --> 16:33.575
Goddamn it.

16:35.911 --> 16:38.080
For God's sake.

16:57.683 --> 16:58.767
DESERTER ELIMINATED

17:01.687 --> 17:02.604
Hey.

17:06.650 --> 17:09.028
DESERTER ELIMINATED

17:59.995 --> 18:01.914
It was a total pro, all right?

18:01.997 --> 18:05.167
The way the jabs came in,
it couldn't have been an amateur.

18:05.250 --> 18:06.877
Anything else you remember?

18:06.960 --> 18:09.129
I couldn't pay attention to anything.

18:09.213 --> 18:11.715
It was dark. I could barely see.

18:11.799 --> 18:14.218
With punches and kicks raining down…

18:19.681 --> 18:21.183
Anyway, that's all.

18:21.266 --> 18:23.185
Be careful how you answer, Ho-jae.

18:24.311 --> 18:27.147
If one thing goes wrong,
you'll end up taking all the blame.

18:29.066 --> 18:31.235
- What, take the blame?
- Why would I?

18:31.318 --> 18:35.155
You went in there to capture an affair
on camera and get good money for it,

18:35.239 --> 18:37.950
which led to a fight
that resulted in death.

18:38.033 --> 18:39.243
- No!
- That's not true!

18:39.326 --> 18:42.538
The only fingerprints we found
at the scene were yours, Mr. Jang.

18:42.621 --> 18:45.207
I told you, he was already dead
when I entered the room.

18:45.290 --> 18:48.460
And the victim's blood was found
all over your clothes too.

18:48.544 --> 18:51.922
I've said it multiple times.
I had a fight with the one who was there!

18:52.005 --> 18:55.342
Yes, exactly.
Ho-jae did beat people up back in the day.

18:55.425 --> 18:57.511
- I saw it for myself. Right?
- Shut up.

18:57.594 --> 19:00.097
But this kid doesn't kill people
or do stuff like that.

19:00.180 --> 19:02.099
You know that, Captain! Am I right?

19:02.182 --> 19:06.311
Didn't I tell you not to fool around
doing private detective stuff?

19:06.395 --> 19:11.650
I told you illegal wiretapping, recording,
and filming are all punishable by law.

19:11.733 --> 19:13.652
Yes, you did tell us, Captain, but--

19:13.735 --> 19:15.904
Look at this stuff.

19:16.697 --> 19:21.451
All these files you've saved on here,
these are all people having affairs.

19:21.535 --> 19:24.329
All this cheating.
They're too embarrassing to even look at.

19:24.413 --> 19:26.665
Yeah, right.
You're perusing them over and over.

19:27.666 --> 19:28.625
Let's be real.

19:29.585 --> 19:32.546
The illegal filming charge alone
will get you both locked up.

19:32.629 --> 19:35.424
Come on, now! That's such a stretch.

19:35.507 --> 19:38.385
Why are you doing this to us?
You know how it is, Captain.

19:39.052 --> 19:41.597
To tell you about us,

19:41.680 --> 19:44.308
we used to trade goods
in the global market.

19:44.391 --> 19:46.768
But in this worldwide economic recession,

19:46.852 --> 19:49.021
we small fries have been
crushed down to dust.

19:49.104 --> 19:51.190
So, to put bread on the table,

19:51.273 --> 19:55.110
we just did some side hustles
very briefly.

19:55.194 --> 19:57.112
Hey, you know us!

19:57.196 --> 19:58.906
You know who we are, Captain!

20:03.493 --> 20:05.370
I'll zip it now and let you two talk.

20:09.333 --> 20:12.377
You should stop now
and tell me what this is really about.

20:13.587 --> 20:14.630
What?

20:14.713 --> 20:18.050
You're trying to scare us
with the whole illegal filming thing,

20:18.133 --> 20:19.927
so you clearly want something.

20:20.969 --> 20:22.387
Tell me what it is.

20:32.856 --> 20:34.024
Find out who this is.

20:35.400 --> 20:36.235
- What?
- What?

20:36.318 --> 20:37.653
Excuse me, Captain.

20:37.736 --> 20:40.948
But the police should be
looking for the criminal.

20:41.031 --> 20:42.282
Why should we…

20:42.366 --> 20:44.534
We have arrested key suspects already.

20:45.118 --> 20:46.370
But you said it was unfair.

20:46.453 --> 20:48.580
What else can you do
but join us on the hunt?

20:48.664 --> 20:50.499
Excuse me, Captain?

20:50.582 --> 20:52.918
But still, this is a bit too--

20:53.001 --> 20:54.753
Why? You can't do it?

20:54.836 --> 21:00.634
Then you, Jang Ho-jae, will be named
the prime suspect of this murder.

21:00.717 --> 21:04.304
And your face and name
will be plastered all over the news.

21:04.388 --> 21:06.515
I didn't kill him!

21:06.598 --> 21:08.767
Yeah, I mean, how unfair is that?

21:08.850 --> 21:12.229
You'll be accused of being the killer
even though you're innocent.

21:12.312 --> 21:14.898
But I still have a job to do, you know.

21:15.482 --> 21:18.485
You were at the scene
at the time the victim was murdered.

21:18.568 --> 21:21.530
So, currently, you are the prime suspect.

21:22.030 --> 21:25.367
To save face, we'll write a report
and send it to the prosecutors.

21:28.287 --> 21:31.707
I never pegged you as that type, Captain,
but did you know

21:32.833 --> 21:34.001
that you're an asshole?

21:34.084 --> 21:35.544
I sure did.

21:37.546 --> 21:40.716
I'll give you ten days.
Find me whatever you can.

21:40.799 --> 21:43.468
Who this person is,
whether it's a woman or a man,

21:43.552 --> 21:46.888
and what kind of crazy psycho they must be
to kill people in such a way.

21:46.972 --> 21:50.475
Tell me now if you can't do it.
If so, I'll have to arrest you right away.

21:50.559 --> 21:51.727
What's your call?

22:06.533 --> 22:10.037
Ho-jae, we're screwed now, aren't we?

22:12.789 --> 22:15.250
Is this okay? They're civilians after all.

22:17.878 --> 22:19.838
And they're up against a serial killer.

22:19.921 --> 22:22.507
Do you remember the creep
we arrested two months ago

22:23.050 --> 22:25.218
when you had just transferred
to Violent Crimes?

22:25.302 --> 22:27.888
The rapist who went after
the female college students?

22:27.971 --> 22:29.765
The one you chased for over three years?

22:29.848 --> 22:30.682
Yeah.

22:31.600 --> 22:32.684
Those two caught him.

22:33.352 --> 22:34.186
What?

22:34.269 --> 22:37.272
That guy, Jang Ho-jae,
is better than he lets on.

22:39.191 --> 22:40.525
Don't worry too much.

22:43.236 --> 22:45.822
JONGNO-GU SERIAL MURDER CASE

22:53.205 --> 22:57.626
OH KI-HOON (29 YEARS OLD)
BODYGUARD AT JEONSEUNG BIOTECH

22:58.752 --> 22:59.836
We aren't open yet.

23:04.800 --> 23:06.551
How can I help you this time?

23:06.635 --> 23:10.138
That Silverbill person. Let me meet them.

23:10.889 --> 23:15.644
What happened to your son is unfortunate,
but there was nothing we could do.

23:17.437 --> 23:20.315
Your deposit for the request
has been refunded.

23:20.399 --> 23:22.984
You can take that money back.

23:23.693 --> 23:24.528
Pardon?

23:24.611 --> 23:27.239
I'd like to find someone else.

23:28.073 --> 23:29.199
And who might that be?

23:29.282 --> 23:31.785
The person who killed my son.

23:32.285 --> 23:35.205
Whoever it was, I have to find them!

23:35.789 --> 23:36.623
Please?

23:41.336 --> 23:42.421
What do you think?

23:44.172 --> 23:47.300
The client desperately wants you
to find his son's killer.

24:14.453 --> 24:15.537
Ho-jae.

24:16.037 --> 24:19.207
Why don't we leave Seoul
for a while instead?

24:19.291 --> 24:21.293
How about Osaka? Or Singapore?

24:21.376 --> 24:23.879
Should we just go all the way to Hawaii?

24:24.546 --> 24:27.924
That would be like admitting
that I'm the killer.

24:28.008 --> 24:30.677
Are you trying to make me
an international fugitive?

24:30.760 --> 24:32.846
No, that's not what I meant.

24:32.929 --> 24:36.558
I'm saying that we should steer away
from the danger for a bit,

24:36.641 --> 24:38.477
in case you get caught up in trouble.

24:39.853 --> 24:41.188
Can you afford plane tickets?

24:41.771 --> 24:44.232
Of course not.
We gotta muster it up together.

24:44.900 --> 24:49.237
Worrying isn't what we need right now.
We have to find a way.

24:49.905 --> 24:51.740
A realistic way.

24:51.823 --> 24:54.409
What realistic way are you suggesting?

24:54.493 --> 24:56.828
Are you actually
going to catch the culprit?

24:57.996 --> 24:58.830
What is this?

24:59.623 --> 25:02.083
First, let's send out that picture
to all our contacts.

25:02.959 --> 25:06.505
We'll take any and all tip-offs
about anyone who looks remotely similar.

25:07.797 --> 25:09.299
You're really going to do this?

25:09.382 --> 25:13.595
My face is going to be on wanted posters
all over the country in ten days.

25:14.763 --> 25:17.641
I want to live a quiet life, Yong-gil.

25:18.808 --> 25:19.851
Help me out.

25:41.498 --> 25:45.502
Why did you have to ask me
for this favor, Grandpa?

25:50.090 --> 25:53.593
HELLO ANTENNAS, REQUESTING TIP-OFFS
ON THE PERSON IN THE PICTURE

25:58.848 --> 26:02.394
URGENTLY NEEDED, PLEASE CONTACT ASAP

26:10.819 --> 26:13.113
- It's delicious.
- Did you bring them?

26:16.992 --> 26:18.660
- Hey, good work.
- Good Lord.

26:19.369 --> 26:20.745
I'm done. Heading out now.

26:22.831 --> 26:24.624
- What?
- Did you see this picture?

26:24.708 --> 26:25.792
What picture?

28:21.449 --> 28:23.118
Ho-jae. It's Sinsa-dong.

28:24.244 --> 28:27.747
They first saw her while taking photos
of the building for a quote last week,

28:27.831 --> 28:29.833
but they saw her a few times after that.

28:29.916 --> 28:34.170
She usually appears right before sunset
and sits there until it gets dark.

28:36.381 --> 28:37.424
Where in Sinsa-dong?

29:21.676 --> 29:23.219
ACCEPTED

29:23.303 --> 29:24.387
What?

29:26.014 --> 29:26.931
SILVERBILL

29:30.101 --> 29:31.019
Are you sure?

29:31.686 --> 29:33.438
You're really going to take this job?

29:34.522 --> 29:35.565
Under one condition.

29:36.191 --> 29:38.693
If I catch the culprit,
I'll hand them over to the cops.

29:39.819 --> 29:42.655
Tell him that I don't take jobs
from people seeking vengeance,

29:43.698 --> 29:46.075
and that I won't take this job
unless he agrees.

29:46.159 --> 29:48.036
What in the world are you thinking?

29:48.661 --> 29:50.455
You've never taken jobs like this.

29:51.331 --> 29:53.583
Now you're going to find
the murderer for him?

29:54.250 --> 29:56.336
I have a few questions of my own as well.

33:05.608 --> 33:06.484
Who are you?

33:11.656 --> 33:14.242
You're not answering me,
so you must be up to something.

33:16.285 --> 33:18.037
Why don't we face each other first?

33:18.997 --> 33:20.581
You'll only get hurt if you move.

33:23.584 --> 33:24.669
Do you know Oh Ki-hoon?

33:25.753 --> 33:26.838
Are you a cop?

33:26.921 --> 33:28.339
I wouldn't say that.

33:30.174 --> 33:32.510
But I'm looking for the culprit
who killed Oh.

33:33.177 --> 33:35.430
You came to the wrong person. It's not me.

33:35.513 --> 33:37.056
Then why were you there?

33:39.017 --> 33:40.435
The person who was there…

33:42.937 --> 33:44.480
that was you, wasn't it?

34:53.049 --> 34:54.801
That was a solid punch.

34:57.512 --> 34:59.055
You are a pro, aren't you?

35:06.229 --> 35:07.730
I won't go easy on you now.

35:07.814 --> 35:10.024
I'm gonna fight with everything I've got.

35:17.532 --> 35:18.366
Why…

35:26.040 --> 35:27.625
I haven't done anything yet.

35:30.920 --> 35:32.004
Master Jang.

35:41.305 --> 35:42.598
Master Jang.

35:46.853 --> 35:49.105
Is it really you?

37:15.608 --> 37:16.609
Interesting.

37:46.764 --> 37:47.640
Soon…

37:49.684 --> 37:51.102
it will be spring again.

38:16.669 --> 38:19.088
WE HAVE ALWAYS BEEN CURIOUS
ABOUT HUMANS

38:19.171 --> 38:22.925
HUMANS, CREATORS OF HISTORY
AND HISTORY ITSELF

38:23.009 --> 38:25.553
THE RECORD OF EXISTENCE

38:28.264 --> 38:29.932
THE RECORD OF EXISTENCE
BY SHIN JI-OH

38:30.016 --> 38:33.436
THE BOOK OF EVOLUTION AND COEXISTENCE

38:33.686 --> 38:36.105
A FUTURE INSPIRED BY HUMANS

38:36.188 --> 38:38.691
A FUTURE BRED FOR HUMANS

38:39.191 --> 38:40.443
WE ADVANCE

38:40.526 --> 38:42.194
AND EVOLVE

38:42.278 --> 38:44.363
ENDLESSLY

38:44.822 --> 38:46.657
THE POTENTIAL OF HUMANS

38:46.741 --> 38:48.993
THE INFINITY OF HUMANKIND

38:50.703 --> 38:53.622
JEONSEUNG BIOTECH

40:37.685 --> 40:38.686
Let us begin.

40:40.020 --> 40:40.938
Yes, sir.

40:41.605 --> 40:44.400
We will begin Experiment A0-67.
